{
	"Site": "Nexus",
	"Id": 20676,
	"Name": "Caramel Reshade- For Vanilla Color",
	"Author": "xiaoleiwen",
	"Description": "[b][u]Installation: [/u]\n<br />[/b]\n<br />[list=1]\n<br />[*]Download and [b]extract[/b] the [b]Caramel Reshade[/b] file.\n<br />[*]Download [b]reshade setup tool [/b]from [b][url=https://reshade.me/]https://reshade.me/[/url]\uFEFF\u00A0[/b] and run the installer.\n<br />[*][b]Browse[/b] and select [b]Stardew Valley [/b](for [b]vanilla game[/b]) or[b] StardewModdingAPI [/b](for [b]modded game[/b]) in your [b]game installation folder[/b]. For example, the correct folder for Steam user is something like: C:&#92;SteamLibrary&#92;steamapps&#92;common&#92;Stardew Valley\n<br />[*]Choose [b]OpenGL[/b].\n<br />[*][b][u][b][Important ! ][/b][/u] \uFEFFBrowse[/b] and [b]select[/b] the Preset file [b]Caramel Reshade.ini [/b]that you have extracted earlier. Proceed until you finish the installation.\n<br />[*][b][u][b][Important ! ][/b][/u] [/b]Copy the [b]\"reshade-shaders\" [/b]folder that you have extracted earlier, and paste on the one that you have installed in your [b]game installation folder[/b] earlier. You have to [b]overwrite [/b]the files when asked.\n<br />[*]If you don't like the wash-out effect of Reshade on the portrait of dialogue UI, download the [b]Dialogue UI Mask[/b] files, and do the following: \n<br />[/list][spoiler]\n<br />1. [b]Dialogue UI Mask [/b]needs to detect certain part of the dialogue UI, hence only works if all of the following conditions are met:\n<br />[list]\n<br />[*][b]Full-screen [/b]or [b]Window Borderless Mode[/b]\n<br />[*][b]UI scale 100% [/b](Not the Zoom Level, you can use any Zoom Level)\n<br />[*][b]Vanilla UI[/b] or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/4697]Vintage Interface V2[/url] or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/13658]DaisyNiko's Earthy Interface[/url]\uFEFF or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/16970]Cozy Accent Interface (Dark Version)[/url]\uFEFF or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/6166]Overgrown Flowery Interface[/url]\uFEFF or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/17323]Lavender Dreams UI[/url]\uFEFFor [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/17912]VPR Inspired UI[/url]\n<br />[*] [b]Screen resolutions[/b]: [b]1920x1080, 2560x1440 [/b]or [b]3840x2160[/b]\n<br />[/list]2. Extract the [b]Dialogue UI Mask[/b] that you have downloaded, and open the folder according to the type of UI and resolution of your game.\n<br />3. Copy the [b]\"reshade-shaders\" [/b]folder, and paste on the one that you have installed in your [b]game installation folder[/b] earlier. You have to [b][b]overwrite[/b][/b] the files when asked.\n<br />\n<br />* If you want to use [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/19513]Changing Skies -- Weather- and Time-Dependent UI[/url]\uFEFF, set to [b]false[/b] for [b]RoundedCorners[/b].\n<br />[/spoiler]\n<br />\n<br />\uFEFF[b][u]Credits [/u][/b]\n<br />Crosire for ReShade\n<br />\n<br />Also special thanks to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/users/70148453?tab=about+me]AirynS[/url] for the name of this reshade, and friends on discord channels for showing interests, and providing feedback and supports.",
